{% doc %}
  A jersey's place in the run, zero padded — 01, 02, and so on.

  Counted from one collection named in theme settings, so a jersey carries the
  same number on the homepage, the shop page and its own page. Working it out
  from whichever list happens to be on screen is what let the homepage and the
  shop disagree: they were counting different collections in different orders.

  Outputs the total instead when `total` is true.

  @param {object} product - The jersey to number.
  @param {boolean} [total] - Return how many are in the run rather than this one's place.

  @example
  {% render 'brand-run-number', product: product %}
{% enddoc %}

{%- liquid
  assign source = settings.run_collection
  if source == blank
    assign source = collections.all
  endif

  if total
    assign number = source.products_count
  else
    assign number = 0
    for item in source.products
      if item.id == product.id
        assign number = forloop.index
        break
      endif
    endfor
  endif
-%}

{{- number | prepend: '0' | slice: -2, 2 -}}
